Reference reconstruction (after Jacobson, Phys.\ Rev.\ Lett.\ 75, 1260 (1995);
verbatim source: arXiv e-print gr-qc/9504004, file 9504004.tex ---
run fetch_ground_truth.py to extract).

We first express the area variation through the Ricci tensor.
Inserting \eqref{eq:theta_expansion} of \Cref{lemma:raychaudhuri} into
\eqref{eq:area_var} of \Cref{def:entropy_ansatz}:
\begin{equation}
\delta \mathcal{A}
= -\int_{\mathcal{H}} \lambda \, R_{ab} k^a k^b \, d\lambda \, d\mathcal{A}.
\label{eq:area_ricci}
\end{equation}
Hence, with \Cref{def:entropy_ansatz} and \Cref{lemma:unruh},
\begin{equation}
T \, dS = \frac{\hbar\kappa}{2\pi} \, \eta \, \delta\mathcal{A}
= -\frac{\hbar\kappa\eta}{2\pi}
\int_{\mathcal{H}} \lambda \, R_{ab} k^a k^b \, d\lambda \, d\mathcal{A}.
\label{eq:tds}
\end{equation}

With the above in mind, we are now ready to prove the main statement:

\begin{proof}[Proof of \Cref{theorem:jacobson}]
Imposing $\delta Q = T \, dS$ and using \Cref{lemma:heat_flux} together with
\eqref{eq:tds}, the integrands must coincide for every pencil of generators.
Since the horizon $\mathcal{H}$ and the null direction $k^a$ at $p$ are
arbitrary,
\begin{equation}
T_{ab} k^a k^b = \frac{\hbar\eta}{2\pi} \, R_{ab} k^a k^b
\qquad \text{for all null } k^a,
\end{equation}
which implies
\begin{equation}
\frac{2\pi}{\hbar\eta} \, T_{ab} = R_{ab} + f \, g_{ab}
\end{equation}
for some scalar function $f$. Taking the divergence and using
\Cref{lemma:conservation},
\begin{equation}
0 = \nabla^a R_{ab} + \nabla_b f
= \tfrac{1}{2} \nabla_b R + \nabla_b f,
\end{equation}
so $f = -\tfrac{1}{2} R + \Lambda$ with $\Lambda$ constant. Therefore
\begin{equation}
R_{ab} - \tfrac{1}{2} R g_{ab} + \Lambda g_{ab}
= \frac{2\pi}{\hbar\eta} \, T_{ab},
\end{equation}
i.e.\ \eqref{eq:einstein} with $G = (4\hbar\eta)^{-1}$.
\end{proof}
